// THE VERDICT CONFINEMENT ON THE CENSUS CARRIERS, EXECUTED. The census derives six verdicts from
// authored evidence, and until CensusVerdict was sealed a later author could simply write the
// verdict and never call the derivation -- five forbidden promotions DETECTED rather than made
// unwritable. The probe forges all six from outside and the compiler refuses each one.
//
// ONE EXPECTED CAUSE, SIX TIMES, AND THAT IS THE POINT: one carrier confines every verdict, so the
// diagnostic names CensusVerdict rather than six sealed wrappers that would have been the same
// concept re-invented six times.
data probe_workload_census_verdict_construction: PrivateWitness = PrivateWitness {
  entry: "dag/test/probe/workload_census_verdict_construction_probe.dag",
  function: "probe_main",
  disposition: RefusalProbe {
    guards: "sole_constructor confinement on strategy.workload_benchmark_suite CensusVerdict: an architecture reading, a baseline admission, a cache condition, a trial authorization, a replay derivation and a gap reading may only be obtained by running the derivation that produces them, never authored by a consuming module",
    expected_causes: [
      "sole_constructor type 'CensusVerdict' cannot be constructed outside its defining module",
    ],
    dissolution: "this row retires ONLY if the confinement is deliberately removed, and the wall goes with it. A green here means a foreign module can mint a census verdict again, which is the exact state the public-workload-census item exists to prevent -- there is nothing to repair, so it is never retired as fixed.",
  },
}

