// THE DATA MAP AND ITS PROVIDER-ROUTE CONSUMER, ENROLLED TOGETHER BECAUSE THEY ARE ONE CLAIM: the
// map's rows are all proposals, and the executing evidence is that the admission gate discriminates
// on them -- a withheld category refuses, the same scope with a carried category admits, and the
// ratified roster, which is empty until the operator's pass, refuses the route outright.
data witness_data_map: PrivateWitness = PrivateWitness {
  entry: "dag/test/claim/data_map_witness_test.dag",
  function: "data_map_witness_main",
  disposition: Enforced,
}

// THE POSTURE REVISION, EXECUTED THROUGH THE ADMISSION THAT READS IT - AND KNOWN RED UNTIL THE
// ADMISSION IT READS IS ON PUBLIC MAIN. strategy.compliance_posture_revision consumes the
// permitted-jurisdiction population and the two restored jurisdiction refusal arms that gunbc#11194
// adds to product.fabric.provider_route and provider_admission; against public main today those
// names do not resolve. The first cut enrolled this Enforced, which review 64844 correctly rejected:
// the roster runs every enforced witness in ONE process, so one unresolved import stops all of them
// running and reporting - a regression of the actuator dressed as honesty about a dependency. This
// carrier is the one the roster already has for exactly that case: it runs alone, it must FAIL, and
// every cause below is grepped for in its own output so the red is this red and not another one.
// ENFORCED, AND THE PATH HERE IS WORTH KEEPING BECAUSE THE OBVIOUS ROUTE WAS WRONG TWICE.
//
// This row was KnownRed on six "name not found" causes waiting for gunbc#11194, and its own annotation
// predicted that the day #11194 landed the row would go STALE and retire in one edit. #11194 landed at
// 4f3df2aa0bf and neither half of that prediction held.
//
// FIRST, IT DRIFTED RATHER THAN GOING STALE. All six names existed, so none of the declared causes could
// fire -- but the entry still did not resolve: the private consumer and this witness both built and matched
// PermittedJurisdictionsEnumerated with a `basis` field, and the arm that LANDED carries first and further
// only. Flipping to Enforced on the strength of "the trigger is satisfied" would have declared a wall
// restored while the entry reded for a reason nobody had written down, which is the inverse of the defect
// the roster's stale-quarantine rule exists to catch. Measuring rather than reasoning is what separated
// those two states, and it is the only thing that could have.
//
// SECOND, THE FIX TOOK A DELETED ASSERTION WITH IT. population_is_the_clearance_roster ended with
// declaration_ref_eq(a: basis, b: m2_posture_ruling), so dropping the field dropped a check. The ruling
// grounds the population through posture_revision_hash -- it is an INPUT to the revision, which is
// structurally stronger than a citation because the two then cannot disagree -- so the claim was re-made at
// that carrier as a_ruling_change_changes_the_revision rather than deleted. Ruling by snappy-pike-154 on
// escalation, whose own #11194 reasoning (that basis duplicated the enclosing authority) held at the two
// public sites and NOT at the private one.
//
// MEASURED before this row was flipped, in that order: resolves and passes, rc=0; and the new conjunct has
// its own red -- giving the varied ruling the SAME quotation makes it fail, naming itself in the output.
data witness_compliance_posture_revision: PrivateWitness = PrivateWitness {
  entry: "dag/test/claim/compliance_posture_revision_witness_test.dag",
  function: "compliance_posture_revision_witness_main",
  disposition: Enforced,
}

